1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,041
Installing Claude Code takes

2
00:00:01,061 --> 00:00:02,980
one command on Windows, Mac and Linux.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,227
On Mac and Linux it's a curl command;

4
00:00:04,247 --> 00:00:05,780
on Windows, PowerShell.

5
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,201
A prompt starting with PS is PowerShell;

6
00:00:08,221 --> 00:00:10,460
without it, it's CMD. Don't mix them up.

7
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:12,683
Homebrew and winget work too,

8
00:00:12,703 --> 00:00:14,710
but they don't auto-update by default.

9
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:17,038
Open a new terminal and run claude --version.

10
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:19,410
If a version number shows up, you're set.

11
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:21,542
Run claude in your project folder.

12
00:00:21,562 --> 00:00:23,310
The first launch asks you to sign in.

13
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,829
You can sign in with a Pro,

14
00:00:24,849 --> 00:00:27,830
Max, Team or Enterprise account, or use an API key.

15
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:30,105
It can access the folder you launch it in and every subfolder;

16
00:00:30,125 --> 00:00:32,780
anything outside needs your permission.

17
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,821
Prefer not to use the terminal? There are editor plugins,

18
00:00:34,841 --> 00:00:36,750
a desktop app, and a web version.

19
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:37,968
Still, the terminal has the fullest feature set,

20
00:00:37,988 --> 00:00:39,830
and some features exist only there.

21
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:41,470
For your first prompt, don't let it edit yet.

22
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:43,880
Press Shift+Tab until the status bar shows plan mode.

23
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,830
Plan mode researches and proposes without

24
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:48,260
editing your source, then hands back a plan.

25
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,325
Once the plan is up,

26
00:00:49,345 --> 00:00:51,980
press Ctrl+G to edit it before you approve.

27
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,434
The official example: dark mode across the whole app,

28
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:55,907
a toggle in the header,

29
00:00:55,927 --> 00:00:58,270
and a good contrast color.

30
00:00:58,290 --> 00:01:00,241
Installing it takes one command.

31
00:01:00,261 --> 00:01:02,470
Using it well starts with Shift+Tab.
